joe_doufu wrote:
> Which part do you consider "the middle"?  This topic has been discussed
> before on this newsgroup, but the usual complaint is that the mid-game
> (after clearing the VoTD, before facing Rodney) is the boring part that
> needs improvement.  As for me, I was bored with Gehennom as soon as I
> entered it the first time, partly because it was built up to be so
> scary.  The "end-game" ascent with the Amulet got kind of fun again,
> and was a challenge.

In my book:
Early game: to the end of the mines or to the quest portal level,
whichever comes first.
Mid game: to the castle.
Late game: castle through the Amulet back up the dungeon to the exit.
End game: Elemental planes and Astral.

The early game is most exciting.  The mid game can be interesting but
the player generally has fewer holes in his inventory.  The late game
is usually quite boring, but once in a while it's tricky.  (Like if
death charges run out and the Wiz must be tackled hand-to-hand, or if
multiple demon lords show up, or if Archons are a problem.)  The late
game is most perilous because the player must survive mostly with the
equipment he takes into it.  Most people who make it that far are
heavily spoiled, so they already know what the best ways of dealing
with the dangers and nasties there are.

